# <%= it.scope %>/oxlint-config

The oxlint rules for every repo that uses <%= it.scope %>: everything in
[`@mfeflow/oxlint-config`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mfeflow/oxlint-config), plus what you put in
`overrides.json`.

`overrides.json` has the same shape as an `oxlintrc.json`. Objects (`rules`, `categories`) are merged key by
key, lists (`plugins`, `ignorePatterns`, `overrides`) are added to, anything else is replaced:

```json
{
  "rules": { "no-console": "error" },
  "ignorePatterns": ["**/generated/**"]
}
```

`pnpm build` writes `dist/oxlintrc.json` from our rules and yours. It is not committed; the release builds it
before publishing, so each release of this package carries the rules of the `@mfeflow/oxlint-config` that was
installed then.

In an app repo:

```json
{
  "extends": ["./node_modules/<%= it.scope %>/oxlint-config/dist/oxlintrc.json"]
}
```

The path is written out because oxlint reads `extends` as a file path and does not look up a package name.
